        {
          "id": 587760871,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It shows both versions in the correct paragraph, this is how almost every other library is handled so far:\n\n>>>\nCompiled (64-bit) **with Qt 5.15.2**, with libpcap, with POSIX capabilities (Linux),\nwith libnl 3, with GLib 2.68.2, with zlib 1.2.11, with Lua 5.2.4, with GnuTLS\n3.7.1 and PKCS \\#11 support, with Gcrypt 1.9.3-unknown, with MIT Kerberos, with\nMaxMind DB resolver, with nghttp2 1.43.0, with brotli, with LZ4, with Zstandard,\nwith Snappy, with libxml2 2.9.10, with SMI 0.5.0, with QtMultimedia, without\nautomatic updates, with SpeexDSP (using system library), with Minizip.\n\nRunning on Linux 5.12.6-arch1-1, with Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8265U CPU @ 1.60GHz\n(with SSE4.2), with 15812 MB of physical memory, with GLib 2.68.2, with zlib\n1.2.11, **with Qt 5.15.2**, with libpcap 1.10.0 (with TPACKET_V3), with c-ares\n1.17.1, with GnuTLS 3.7.1, with Gcrypt 1.9.3-unknown, with nghttp2 1.43.0, with\nbrotli 1.0.9, with LZ4 1.9.3, with Zstandard 1.5.0, with libsmi 0.5.0, with\nlocale LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8, LC_NUMERIC=pt_PT.UTF-8, LC_TIME=pt_PT.UTF-8,\nLC_COLLATE=en_US.UTF-8, LC_MONETARY=pt_PT.UTF-8, LC_MESSAGES=en_US.UTF-8,\nLC_PAPER=pt_PT.UTF-8, LC_NAME=en_US.UTF-8, LC_ADDRESS=en_US.UTF-8,\nLC_TELEPHONE=en_US.UTF-8, LC_MEASUREMENT=pt_PT.UTF-8,\nLC_IDENTIFICATION=en_US.UTF-8, binary plugins supported (0 loaded).\n\nBuilt using gcc 11.1.0.\n>>>\n\nRunning with and compiled with versions happen to be the same in my case.",
