        {
          "id": 587787993,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "From the prospect of a Qt developer, I see very little benefit in adding the runtime version as well. Hardly any issues ever occur because those two differ. Also, for end-user development we alread supply our own version in the packages anyhow or set them as dependency. With Qt 6 we might see a benefit, as multiple distributions may exist, but even there I don't really see this becoming an issue.\n\nI retract my disapproval, feel free to merge if you want to, I just don't see the point and think this information is redundant and might also lead to scenarios where user accidently forward the runtime version on issue reports instead of the more important build version.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
